ter. \n\nWait, but if I discard W5, the sequence is broken. However, if I keep W5, I have a complete Chow. So maybe it's better to keep the Chow. \n\nIn that case, maybe discard a tile that's not part of a sequence. Like J3. \n\nYes, J3 is a single tile. Discarding it might not help others as much. \n\nSo the answer would be Play J3.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard the White Dragon (J3) as it is a single tile not part of any sequence and reduces the risk of aiding opponents' melds.  \nReason: Discarding J3 avoids completing potential pungs for others, while retaining key tiles (W3-4-5) for a possible chow and maintaining flexibility in hand development.  \nAnswer: Play J3"}
